From dfe81a29bb4d85fd50f677d0d82c3d30fd008af8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangjianxin <wangjianxin@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Mar 2026 10:57:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: k230: Fix composite mux clobber and add
 CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT

Trimmed from upstream 06f5feb. The original commit also renamed clock
nodes in k230_clock_provider.dtsi (cosmetic only) and added
clk_set_rate(800M) calls in drivers/misc/canaan/gnne/k230_gnne.c. Those
hunks are dropped here:

  - dtsi renames fail to apply (line numbers shifted on this kernel SHA)
    and are functionally a no-op.
  - k230_gnne.c hunks depend on ai_enable_power_and_clk() which is added
    by upstream's 0014-Add-clock-and-power-domain-support-for-AI-...patch,
    which we deliberately do not carry on the small-core branch (no
    AI/NN stack).

What remains is the general-purpose clock-driver fix:

  - k230_clk_composite_set_parent() now preserves the bits of the
    composite gate register that are not part of the mux field, instead
    of overwriting the whole register. Without this fix, reprogramming
    the parent of any composite clock on the K230 clobbers the gate
    bits of unrelated clocks sharing the same register.
  - Add CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT to the composite clock init flags so
    rate-change requests do not silently change the parent.

This is what we care about for the small-core/AMP work: the SHRM AXI
master clock (which feeds gsdma_aclk_gate / nonai2d_aclk_gate /
pdma_aclk_gate) is a composite, and the Linux-side AMP launcher will
need to manipulate its descendants without disturbing neighbouring
gates.
---
 drivers/clk/clk-k230.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 drivers/clk/clk-k230.c

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c b/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index 71d38f7d4..ac022ef1e
--- a/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
@@ -499,6 +499,8 @@ static int k230_clk_composite_set_parent(struct clk_hw *hw, u8 index)
 				  << k230_composite->mux_shift;

 	spin_lock_irqsave(k230_composite->composite_spinlock, flags);
+	composite_mux_value |= readl(k230_composite->gate_reg) &
+		    ~(k230_composite->mux_mask << k230_composite->mux_shift);
 	writel(composite_mux_value, k230_composite->mux_reg);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(k230_composite->composite_spinlock, flags);

@@ -765,7 +767,7 @@ static struct clk *_of_cannan_k230_clk_composite_setup(struct device_node *node)
 	init.parent_names = parent_name;
 	init.name = node->name;
 	init.ops = p_clk_ops;
-	init.flags = CLK_IS_BASIC /*|flags*/;
+	init.flags = CLK_IS_BASIC | CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT/*|flags*/;
 	k230_clk_composite->hw.init = &init;

 	hw = &k230_clk_composite->hw;
--
2.25.1
